1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,949
December ninth, nineteen sixty-five.

2
00:00:02,949 --> 00:00:05,638
A small town in western Pennsylvania.

3
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:14,213
By nightfall the woods outside it are full of flashlights, state police, and a rumor that something fell from the sky.

4
00:00:14,213 --> 00:00:15,666
Was it a spacecraft?

5
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:25,874
The legend says it was shaped like an acorn, the size of a small car, ringed with strange writing, and hauled away on a flatbed truck.

6
00:00:25,874 --> 00:00:29,000
Television calls it Pennsylvania's Roswell.

7
00:00:29,466 --> 00:00:38,022
So tonight we rebuild that evening minute by minute, from newspapers, seismographs, court records and the people who were there.

8
00:00:38,022 --> 00:00:40,094
Only what we can verify counts.

9
00:00:40,094 --> 00:00:42,166
This is the Kecksburg incident.

10
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:43,988
The Kecksburg acorn.

11
00:00:43,988 --> 00:00:45,615
Evidence against theory.

12
00:00:45,615 --> 00:00:46,700
Start the clock.

13
00:00:51,166 --> 00:00:53,756
Four forty-three p.m., eastern time.

14
00:00:53,756 --> 00:00:56,777
Over Michigan and Ontario, people look up.

15
00:00:56,777 --> 00:01:03,899
A fireball, brighter than anything they have seen, is crossing the darkening sky from west to east.

16
00:01:04,366 --> 00:01:09,387
At least twenty-three pilots report it, the first at four forty-four.

17
00:01:09,387 --> 00:01:13,025
It is seen across six American states and Ontario.

18
00:01:13,025 --> 00:01:14,771
This part is not legend.

19
00:01:14,771 --> 00:01:16,299
It is in the records.

20
00:01:16,766 --> 00:01:21,382
Near Detroit, a seismograph picks up shock waves from the sky.

21
00:01:21,382 --> 00:01:24,732
Sonic booms rattle windows around Pittsburgh.

22
00:01:24,732 --> 00:01:28,454
A fireball that loud and that long is not a rumor.

23
00:01:28,454 --> 00:01:30,166
It is a physical event.

24
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:34,278
Astronomers gather the sightings and a few photographs.

25
00:01:34,278 --> 00:01:41,833
Their reconstruction, published in nineteen sixty-seven, is the best data we have on where the object really went.

26
00:01:42,299 --> 00:01:44,997
And then the landing reports begin.

27
00:01:44,997 --> 00:01:46,693
Hot metal in Michigan.

28
00:01:46,693 --> 00:01:48,235
Grass fires in Ohio.

29
00:01:48,235 --> 00:01:53,400
Each witness places the object close by, just beyond the next hill.

30
00:01:53,866 --> 00:01:58,383
Geophysicist George Wetherill explained why in Sky and Telescope.

31
00:01:58,383 --> 00:02:02,899
Almost everyone thought the fireball was much closer than it was.

32
00:02:02,899 --> 00:02:07,833
When it slipped behind a tree, they thought it had dropped just beyond.

33
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:11,673
So scientists drew one line through all of it.

34
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,973
One continuous track, hundreds of miles long.

35
00:02:14,973 --> 00:02:18,566
A single object, moving fast, burning in the air.

36
00:02:19,033 --> 00:02:21,789
Now zoom in on one spot on that line.

37
00:02:21,789 --> 00:02:28,047
Kecksburg, Pennsylvania, a small village about thirty miles southeast of Pittsburgh.

38
00:02:28,047 --> 00:02:32,666
A volunteer fire department, a few houses, and a lot of woods.

39
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:34,391
It is dinner time.

40
00:02:34,391 --> 00:02:37,397
Families see the light pass over the hills.

41
00:02:37,397 --> 00:02:40,123
Some say it slowed, turned and dropped.

42
00:02:40,123 --> 00:02:42,500
Others only felt the ground thump.

43
00:02:42,966 --> 00:02:44,789
Some run up into the woods.

44
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:47,558
They report blue smoke between the trees.

45
00:02:47,558 --> 00:02:53,500
In the village, people talk about a vibration, and a sound like something heavy landing.

46
00:02:53,966 --> 00:02:55,783
The calls start coming in.

47
00:02:55,783 --> 00:03:00,815
To the state police, to the local radio, to the newspaper in Greensburg.

48
00:03:00,815 --> 00:03:04,099
Everyone has the same question: what came down?

49
00:03:04,566 --> 00:03:06,064
Four forty-six p.m.

50
00:03:06,064 --> 00:03:11,424
is the time some accounts give for something landing near Kecksburg.

51
00:03:11,424 --> 00:03:15,444
NASA's own catalog calls these unconfirmed reports.

52
00:03:15,444 --> 00:03:17,099
Hold on to that word.

53
00:03:17,566 --> 00:03:23,337
By dark, firemen, state troopers and neighbors are searching the woods with flashlights.

54
00:03:23,337 --> 00:03:25,238
They are looking for a wreck.

55
00:03:25,238 --> 00:03:29,566
What they actually find is the subject of sixty years of argument.

56
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:32,308
This is where the legend begins.

57
00:03:32,308 --> 00:03:41,762
Witnesses later described a metallic object half buried in the leaves, shaped like an acorn, with a band of markings around its base.

58
00:03:41,762 --> 00:03:42,900
We will test it.

59
00:03:43,366 --> 00:03:45,927
Here is the problem with the legend.

60
00:03:45,927 --> 00:03:47,990
The evidence comes in layers.

61
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:50,978
Layer one is December nineteen sixty-five.

62
00:03:50,978 --> 00:03:53,326
Layer two is memory, years later.

63
00:03:53,326 --> 00:03:55,033
We will keep them apart.

64
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,539
Now the cordon.

65
00:03:56,539 --> 00:04:02,846
The legend says soldiers arrived within hours, sealed the woods and carried something away.

66
00:04:02,846 --> 00:04:06,866
So what does the nineteen sixty-five record actually show?

67
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:10,591
The Greensburg Tribune-Review, December tenth.

68
00:04:10,591 --> 00:04:15,266
Authorities had sealed off a patch of woods to wait for engineers.

69
00:04:15,266 --> 00:04:20,366
It is the strongest contemporary support for the legend, and it is real.

70
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:24,623
The next edition reports Searchers Fail to Find Object.

71
00:04:24,623 --> 00:04:32,066
Troopers and Air Force personnel with Geiger counters walk the woods, find nothing, and call off the search.

72
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:34,333
So the Air Force was there.

73
00:04:34,333 --> 00:04:35,533
That part is true.

74
00:04:35,533 --> 00:04:38,133
The question is what they were hunting.

75
00:04:38,133 --> 00:04:45,733
A Soviet space probe had been stranded in orbit for two weeks, and it was due to fall back to Earth that same day.

76
00:04:46,199 --> 00:04:54,470
That probe was Kosmos ninety-six, a Venus mission launched on November twenty-third that never left Earth orbit.

77
00:04:54,470 --> 00:05:01,633
Researcher James Oberg proposed it as the Kecksburg object, and the coincidence of dates is real.

78
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:05,246
But NASA's own catalog says it does not fit.

79
00:05:05,246 --> 00:05:12,468
Air Force tracking puts the probe's orbital decay earlier than twenty-one forty-three universal time.

80
00:05:12,468 --> 00:05:15,399
That is the exact minute of the fireball.

81
00:05:15,866 --> 00:05:21,744
Even Leslie Kean, the journalist who pushed hardest for the files, says data from U.S.

82
00:05:21,744 --> 00:05:26,665
Space Command and the Russian space agency rule out a Russian satellite.

83
00:05:26,665 --> 00:05:30,766
The leading earthly candidate is in trouble from both sides.

84
00:05:31,233 --> 00:05:35,574
Researcher Stan Gordon began collecting accounts soon after.

85
00:05:35,574 --> 00:05:45,847
He says multiple independent witnesses saw a metallic, acorn-shaped object on the ground, and that the military arrived quickly to recover it.

86
00:05:45,847 --> 00:05:47,366
He remains convinced.

87
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:56,271
Skeptical researchers who combed the nineteen sixty-five papers say no account from that time mentions anything being recovered.

88
00:05:56,271 --> 00:06:02,666
The Tribune-Review editors wrote on December eleventh that nothing at all seems to have happened.

89
00:06:03,133 --> 00:06:13,353
The flatbed story comes mainly from one witness, John Hays, who was ten in nineteen sixty-five and who told it on television in nineteen ninety.

90
00:06:13,353 --> 00:06:17,966
He described a truck carrying something the size of a Volkswagen.

91
00:06:18,433 --> 00:06:24,449
Contemporary reports describe a short search, a couple of hours, and an empty result.

92
00:06:24,449 --> 00:06:27,210
A secret recovery is not in the record.

93
00:06:27,210 --> 00:06:30,466
It first appears a quarter of a century later.

94
00:06:30,933 --> 00:06:35,510
So if nothing solid was carried out of those woods, what was that light?

95
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:39,133
The morning after, the astronomers already had an answer.

96
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,670
December tenth.

97
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:47,375
The Air Force and the Defense Department say it was a natural phenomenon, a meteor or meteors.

98
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:50,443
Astronomers at several observatories agree.

99
00:06:50,443 --> 00:06:54,366
It is the official answer, and it arrives within a day.

100
00:06:54,833 --> 00:07:08,133
In nineteen sixty-seven, two astronomers published a detailed reconstruction in the Journal of the Royal Astronomical Society of Canada, using the seismograph record and photographs of the trail.

101
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:16,543
Their reconstruction places the end of the track near the northwest shore of Lake Erie, close to Windsor, Ontario.

102
00:07:16,543 --> 00:07:19,399
That is hundreds of miles from Kecksburg.

103
00:07:19,866 --> 00:07:24,466
If that is right, the fireball burned out well short of Pennsylvania.

104
00:07:24,466 --> 00:07:27,066
Nothing solid came down in those woods.

105
00:07:27,066 --> 00:07:31,066
People saw the end of the light, and the hills did the rest.

106
00:07:31,533 --> 00:07:33,419
A bolide, in other words.

107
00:07:33,419 --> 00:07:35,003
A very bright meteor.

108
00:07:35,003 --> 00:07:40,435
Some astronomers even suggested a Geminid, since that shower was active.

109
00:07:40,435 --> 00:07:42,924
Most of these burn up completely.

110
00:07:42,924 --> 00:07:47,300
The few that do not scatter small stones, not tidy acorns.

111
00:07:47,766 --> 00:07:50,170
The official answer has a weakness.

112
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:55,321
None of our sources identifies a single recovered fragment from that night.

113
00:07:55,321 --> 00:07:57,244
A meteor explains the light.

114
00:07:57,244 --> 00:08:00,266
It does not explain the thump and the smoke.

115
00:08:00,733 --> 00:08:05,532
A second earthly idea: a classified American re-entry vehicle.

116
00:08:05,532 --> 00:08:11,880
In twenty fifteen, two MUFON researchers argued for one built by General Electric.

117
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,351
It is a hypothesis.

118
00:08:13,351 --> 00:08:17,066
Neither NASA nor the Air Force has confirmed it.

119
00:08:17,533 --> 00:08:18,930
Then the Nazi bell.

120
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:27,973
Television shows in the late two-thousands pushed a story of a secret German device called Die Glocke falling in Kecksburg.

121
00:08:27,973 --> 00:08:30,399
No documents tie it to the event.

122
00:08:30,866 --> 00:08:38,317
That leaves four stories: a meteor, a Soviet probe, a secret American vehicle, and a craft from elsewhere.

123
00:08:38,317 --> 00:08:41,200
Only the first has a measured trajectory.

124
00:08:41,666 --> 00:08:44,529
But the acorn did not come from the sky.

125
00:08:44,529 --> 00:08:46,247
It came from television.

126
00:08:46,247 --> 00:08:48,466
Fast forward twenty-five years.

127
00:08:48,933 --> 00:08:50,873
December nineteen ninety.

128
00:08:50,873 --> 00:08:56,615
NBC's Unsolved Mysteries airs a Kecksburg episode, hosted by Robert Stack.

129
00:08:56,615 --> 00:09:03,600
It features an acorn-shaped object, hieroglyph-like writing, and a secret military pickup.

130
00:09:04,066 --> 00:09:07,166
To film it, the producers built a prop acorn.

131
00:09:07,166 --> 00:09:13,364
It still stands by the Kecksburg fire station, and visitors take their pictures beside it.

132
00:09:13,364 --> 00:09:15,500
It is a mockup, not the object.

133
00:09:15,966 --> 00:09:17,466
Here is what changed.

134
00:09:17,466 --> 00:09:21,609
In nineteen sixty-five the stories were smoke and a thump.

135
00:09:21,609 --> 00:09:25,680
After the show, they were a craft, markings and soldiers.

136
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:29,538
Gordon says his interviews recorded the acorn earlier.

137
00:09:29,538 --> 00:09:31,966
Skeptics say the papers never did.

138
00:09:32,433 --> 00:09:42,493
Skeptics Joe Nickell and Tom McGaha call this the Roswellian syndrome: witness accounts that grow with each retelling over the decades.

139
00:09:42,493 --> 00:09:44,431
Memory is not a recording.

140
00:09:44,431 --> 00:09:46,666
It is a story we keep editing.

141
00:09:47,133 --> 00:09:48,459
Locals were furious.

142
00:09:48,459 --> 00:09:58,733
According to the Tribune-Review, more than fifty residents, roughly ten percent of the town, signed a petition asking the producers not to air the program.

143
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:07,473
Fire chief Ed Myers, named in the legend as helping seal the woods, told the paper there was absolutely no truth to it.

144
00:10:07,473 --> 00:10:13,799
Defenders reply that locals were embarrassed, and a quiet recovery would not make the news.

145
00:10:14,266 --> 00:10:16,954
That last argument cannot be tested.

146
00:10:16,954 --> 00:10:19,343
And the retelling never stopped.

147
00:10:19,343 --> 00:10:27,333
In two thousand three the Sci Fi Channel aired The New Roswell: Kecksburg Exposed, hosted by Bryant Gumbel.

148
00:10:27,799 --> 00:10:32,550
UFO Hunters, Close Encounters and Ancient Aliens retold it too.

149
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:34,661
Each telling added a little.

150
00:10:34,661 --> 00:10:41,899
By then, the fireball of nineteen sixty-five was only the first sentence of a much bigger story.

151
00:10:42,366 --> 00:10:44,534
Meanwhile, a real paper trail.

152
00:10:44,534 --> 00:10:57,399
In January two thousand three, journalist Leslie Kean, working with the Coalition for Freedom of Information and backed by the Sci Fi Channel, asked NASA for its Kecksburg files.

153
00:10:57,866 --> 00:10:58,572
Kean sued.

154
00:10:58,572 --> 00:11:06,051
By March two thousand seven, a federal court found NASA's first searches inadequate, and NASA admitted it.

155
00:11:06,051 --> 00:11:11,766
In October, a settlement required a new search and the payment of her legal fees.

156
00:11:12,233 --> 00:11:14,655
Hundreds of new documents arrived.

157
00:11:14,655 --> 00:11:19,216
The court-monitored search finished in August two thousand nine.

158
00:11:19,216 --> 00:11:25,700
Kean's conclusion: no smoking gun, but contradictions, and many files missing or destroyed.

159
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:29,218
Skeptics read the same pages differently.

160
00:11:29,218 --> 00:11:35,173
NASA does not investigate UFOs, so its files were never the right place to look.

161
00:11:35,173 --> 00:11:41,500
Lost paper in sixty-year-old government storage is ordinary, not proof of a cover-up.

162
00:11:41,966 --> 00:11:51,637
Kean told Space.com she is convinced something came down at Kecksburg, and that a UFO or a secret American device cannot be ruled out.

163
00:11:51,637 --> 00:11:56,833
She added that the real lesson was about the Freedom of Information Act.

164
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:04,539
Gordon, who has studied the case for decades, and Kean, who sued over it, still call it an open question.

165
00:12:04,539 --> 00:12:05,986
That honesty matters.

166
00:12:05,986 --> 00:12:08,400
It also is not evidence of a craft.

167
00:12:08,866 --> 00:12:10,352
Time to score the case.

168
00:12:10,352 --> 00:12:13,066
Evidence on one side, theory on the other.

169
00:12:13,533 --> 00:12:19,701
A fireball over six states with at least twenty-three pilot reports: evidence.

170
00:12:19,701 --> 00:12:22,786
Shock waves on a seismograph: evidence.

171
00:12:22,786 --> 00:12:25,237
A natural meteor: the best fit.

172
00:12:25,237 --> 00:12:29,666
Cosmos ninety-six: doubtful, even by NASA's own catalog.

173
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:36,505
An acorn-shaped craft: unverified, first described in detail in nineteen ninety.

174
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:41,204
A military recovery on a flatbed: no contemporary evidence.

175
00:12:41,204 --> 00:12:43,833
An alien spacecraft: no evidence.

176
00:12:44,299 --> 00:12:45,142
The verdict.

177
00:12:45,142 --> 00:12:45,915
Not aliens.

178
00:12:45,915 --> 00:12:56,798
Something real lit the sky on December ninth, nineteen sixty-five, and the best-supported answer is a bright meteor that burned up well short of Kecksburg.

179
00:12:56,798 --> 00:13:01,433
The acorn and the flatbed rest on memories recorded decades later.

180
00:13:01,899 --> 00:13:03,847
But be honest about the gaps.

181
00:13:03,847 --> 00:13:11,771
A search happened, the files are incomplete, and nobody has shown publicly what, if anything, the Air Force recovered.

182
00:13:11,771 --> 00:13:15,666
Partly open is a fair label for what the records leave us.

183
00:13:16,133 --> 00:13:21,437
What stays with me is how a thump and some blue smoke became an acorn.

184
00:13:21,437 --> 00:13:23,331
Stories improve with age.

185
00:13:23,331 --> 00:13:29,166
The fireball itself, wide, loud and seen by thousands, never needed any help.

186
00:13:29,633 --> 00:13:37,350
Next case: a Norwegian valley where glowing orbs have appeared for decades, and scientists are still studying them.

187
00:13:37,350 --> 00:13:39,899
Mystery lights, or something stranger?

188
00:13:40,366 --> 00:13:42,671
What do you think fell near Kecksburg?

189
00:13:42,671 --> 00:13:47,766
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
